      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims P-R normally shows normal pressure in RHOB service station based on area directory definition of scope and custodian role; however the evidence (IA-D01) explicitly states the directory is a location index that does not establish valve positions or pressure availability at any given time. The claim conflates 'defined operating scope' with 'established current condition'.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A record showing P-R was in normal band prior to 10:00 AM (e.g., shift log entry, operator screen capture) that is not merely a directory definition.",
      "question": "What specific evidence confirms the pressure at point P-R was within the normal band immediately before the incident?"
    },
    "node-1qg9315": {
      "supported": true,
      "issue": "",
      "evidenceNeeded": "",
      "question": ""
    },
    "node-l8j53n": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims the field execution record was blank at folder issue; while IA-S02 confirms 'WO-527-E | Blank at folder issue', this does not prove that no initial valve-by-valve status or isolation checklist existed in practice. The claim interprets a blank administrative field as proof of missing physical documentation, which is an inference requiring additional evidence.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Evidence showing whether the crew actually performed and recorded any valve checks before 10:00 AM despite the blank form (e.g., handwritten notes, verbal confirmation logs).",
      "question": "Did the Utilities team document actual valve states or isolation steps in a non-formal way when WO-527-E was issued?"
    }
  },
  "decision": {
    "summary": "Three nodes require revision. Node-bywgij is unsupported because it treats an index definition as proof of current pressure condition. Node-l8j53n is unsupported because a blank administrative field does not prove absence of physical documentation or procedure execution; the causal link between 'blank form' and 'no valve status recorded' needs corroboration.",
    "evidenceUsed": ["IA-D01_area_and_service_directory.md", "IA-S02_work_package_cover.md"],
    "unknowns": [
      "Actual pressure state at P-R before 10:00 AM",
      "Whether valve states were documented outside the blank WO-527-E form"
    ],
    "alternatives": [
      "Pressure was normal but not recorded; interruption occurred downstream.",
      "Valves were checked verbally and not written down, making 'blank field' a false indicator of missing procedure."
    ],"confidence": 0.85}
